phase P5
title Hosts, Stories, and CLI

tasks
    T501
        title        Existing Runtime provider
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@task.Rewrite.T201]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.ReactAndHosts.O1,
                     @plan.ReactAndHosts.V1,
                     @plan.ReactAndHosts.D1,
                     @plan.ReactAndHosts.C1
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.ReactAndHosts.O1]
        description
            Deliverable: FlowProvider consumes one already-created Runtime and its cached readiness.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/react/provider/** and co-located tests.
            Evidence: provider tests and workflow/tasks/Rewrite/evidence/T501.md.
            1. Implement the sole React context provider with runtime-only props.
            2. Cache Runtime readiness without acquiring services or disposal ownership.
            3. Test explicit nested and concurrent Runtime isolation.
            Prerequisite: P2 T201 establishes no-persistence Runtime readiness. T502 consumes the
            provider context; it must not create or replace provider authority.
            Shared-write boundary: T501 owns provider files. T601 alone owns package route files.
        acceptance
            The exact <FlowProvider runtime={runtime}> form typechecks; App, Implementation, boot,
            factory, actor ID, storage, codec, and restore props reject.
            Nested unrelated Runtimes retain separate lookup, subscriptions, lifecycle, and state.
            Readiness failure remains visible and no second Runtime or cleanup owner is created.
            Run the focused provider tests and flow-state-rewrite check:types; expected: pass.

    T502
        title        React actor preparation and attachment
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [
                     @task.Rewrite.T201,
                     @task.Rewrite.T202,
                     @task.Rewrite.T203,
                     @task.Rewrite.T204,
                     @task.Rewrite.T207,
                     @task.Rewrite.T208,
                     @task.Rewrite.T209,
                     @task.Rewrite.T210,
                     @T501
                     ]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.ReactAndHosts.O2,
                     @plan.ReactAndHosts.V2,
                     @plan.ReactAndHosts.D1,
                     @plan.ReactAndHosts.C1
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.ReactAndHosts.O2]
        description
            Deliverable: useActor and useActorByRef attach existing production actor ownership
            safely.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/react/actor/** and co-located tests.
            Evidence: preparation, commit, lifecycle, and type tests; evidence/T502.md.
            1. Prepare one fresh actor ref, snapshot, command-only handle, and bounded mailbox per
            component incarnation without render-time registration or work.
            2. Commit against the exact provider revision and attach the same prepared actor.
            3. Exercise abandonment, changed construction tuples, Strict Mode, Activity, and ref
            lookup.
            Prerequisites: P2 admission, lease, lifecycle, context, mailbox, macrostep, timer, and
            actor-snapshot owners establish the production seams. T501 establishes provider
            identity.
            Shared-write boundary: T502 owns actor hooks. T503 consumes the handle and snapshot
            types.
        acceptance
            Abandoned render creates no registration, Scope, subscription, work, persistence write,
            or
            evidence; its mailbox closes once and later commands reject.
            Commit attaches the same actor and silently replaces stale provisional context.
            The mailbox accepts at least 64 commands and overflow rejects without mutation.
            Strict Mode and Activity preserve identity; suspension rejects commands and waits for
            finalizers before resuming without replay. useActorByRef never creates or leases actors.
            Run focused browser lifecycle/type tests; expected: all specified cases pass.

    T503
        title        Passive React selectors
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [
                     @T502,
                     @task.Rewrite.T303,
                     @task.Rewrite.T305,
                     @task.Rewrite.T313
                     ]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.ReactAndHosts.O3,
                     @plan.ReactAndHosts.V3,
                     @plan.ReactAndHosts.D2,
                     @plan.ReactAndHosts.C1
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.ReactAndHosts.O3]
        description
            Deliverable: useView observes exact actor and StoreFanout truth without gaining
            authority.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/react/view/** and co-located tests.
            Evidence: selector types, dependency, equality, failure, and tear-free tests;
            evidence/T503.md.
            1. Implement exact descriptor/key dependency tracking and replace dependencies per run.
            2. Apply the fixed Object.is scalar and named-record rules plus useShallow.
            3. Test store/actor publication races, conditional reads, defects, and forbidden inputs.
            Prerequisites: T502 supplies exact actor handles; P3 T303/T305/T313 supply canonical
            reads,
            writes, and integrated publication. No selector may add a competing store subscription.
            Shared-write boundary: T503 owns selector implementation and tests; T601 owns exports.
        acceptance
            Selectors track only reads from the latest evaluation and return one tear-free
            committed cut.
            Scalar and non-null plain named-record equality follows the fixed Object.is rules.
            Selector identity change preserves actor subscription; matching store publications
            update it.
            Machine, ref, comparator, mutation, and broad-subscription forms reject in type/runtime
            tests.
            Exceptions memoize at an unchanged cut and retry only after a matching publication.
            Run focused selector tests and check:types; expected: pass without mutation or work.

    T504
        title        SSR and isolated request hosts
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [
                     @T502,
                     @task.Rewrite.T402,
                     @task.Rewrite.T403,
                     @task.Rewrite.T404
                     ]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.ReactAndHosts.O4,
                     @plan.ReactAndHosts.V1,
                     @plan.ReactAndHosts.V2,
                     @plan.ReactAndHosts.C2,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O2,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O3,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O4,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.V2,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.V3,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.V4
                     ]
        description
            Deliverable: server preparation stays inert and each request uses its own production
            Runtime.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/react/hosts/** and co-located tests.
            Evidence: server render, concurrent request, hydration, and cleanup receipts;
            evidence/T504.md.
            1. Integrate SSR with the same prepared actor and commit attachment laws as React
            clients.
            2. Use request-owned RuntimeSetup, typed events, production operation kernels, and
            cleanup.
            3. Test concurrent requests, abandoned renders, restored context, and cleanup failures.
            Prerequisites: T502 owns preparation/attachment; P4 T402-T404 own detached boot,
            capture,
            and hydration. P4-specific semantics remain with those owner Tasks.
            Shared-write boundary: T504 owns server/request adapters, not persistence internals or
            routes.
        acceptance
            Abandoned server rendering closes its mailbox and performs no registration or work.
            A committed host attaches the same prepared actor and drains commands once.
            Concurrent requests and the browser share no Runtime, actor, lease, state, or
            persistence.
            Hydration installs provider-derived context without input, initializer, event, or
            context-event
            replay. Each request disposes exactly its Runtime and preserves handler/cleanup failure
            truth.
            Run focused server/browser tests; expected: isolation and no-replay cases pass.

    T505
        title        Effect bridges and construction-owned writes
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [
                     @task.Rewrite.T105,
                     @task.Rewrite.T106,
                     @task.Rewrite.T201,
                     @task.Rewrite.T204,
                     @task.Rewrite.T305
                     ]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.ReactAndHosts.O4,
                     @plan.ReactAndHosts.V4,
                     @plan.ReactAndHosts.D1,
                     @plan.ReactAndHosts.C1
                     ]
        description
            Deliverable: final Effect bridges and private construction-scoped writes preserve
            installed
            Runtime authority and exact failure channels.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/react/bridges/** and co-located tests.
            Evidence: bridge typing, cause, revocation, and pre-mutation tests; evidence/T505.md.
            1. Implement runPromise/runPromiseExit over the installed application Context and exact
            A/E/R.
            2. Adapt foreign Promises once at named boundaries and preserve complete Cause.
            3. Test construction-scoped write authority against wrong, stale, revoked, and valid
            cases.
            Prerequisites: P1 diagnostics and operation seams, P2 readiness/context, and P3
            canonical writes
            own the failures and store mutation boundary. No public HostWriteLease is added.
            Shared-write boundary: T505 owns bridge adapters; T504 owns request hosts; routes stay
            in T601.
        acceptance
            runPromiseExit resolves Exit with the specified typed bridge failure; readiness failure
            stays
            inside Exit and complete Cause reaches the terminal owner.
            Foreign Promise rejection maps once to the owned typed failure and supported abort is
            forwarded.
            Invalid construction authority fails before store mutation or publication; closing
            Scope revokes it.
            No public constructor, callable lease, nested Effect runner, or second Scope is
            introduced.
            Run focused bridge and negative type tests; expected: all pass.

    T506
        title        Closed inert Story builders
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [
                     @task.Rewrite.T101,
                     @task.Rewrite.T102,
                     @task.Rewrite.T103,
                     @task.Rewrite.T104,
                     @task.Rewrite.T105,
                     @task.Rewrite.T106
                     ]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.StoriesAndModels.O1,
                     @plan.StoriesAndModels.V1,
                     @plan.StoriesAndModels.C1
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.StoriesAndModels.O1]
        description
            Deliverable: machine and App Story builders retain exact literals and create no Runtime
            work.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/testing/story/** and co-located tests.
            Evidence: isolated type fixtures and constructor tests; evidence/T506.md.
            1. Implement only the accepted closed constructor and command forms from the Plan.
            2. Prove checkpoint-name accumulation, exact inferred requirements, and persistent
            branching.
            3. Reject excluded constructors, fields, and command names in strict consumers.
            Prerequisite: P1 owns definition/machine/App/Implementation/diagnostic and operation
            seams.
            Shared-write boundary: T506 owns DSL types; later Story Tasks own separate
            execution/model
            modules and must not widen this public constructor surface.
        acceptance
            Builders preserve exact App/machine/recipe options, void input, checkpoint names, and
            service
            requirement closure in isolated declaration consumers.
            Construction acquires no services, Runtime, fixture, actor, sink, or evidence.
            Rejected fields and legacy commands fail type checks; each prefix extension leaves its
            source
            unchanged and creates isolated persistent branches.
            Run testing check:types, check:packed-consumers, and focused constructor tests;
            expected: pass.

    T507
        title        Story fixtures and exact actor recipes
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [
                     @T506,
                     @task.Rewrite.T103,
                     @task.Rewrite.T104,
                     @task.Rewrite.T106,
                     @task.Rewrite.T202,
                     @task.Rewrite.T203,
                     @task.Rewrite.T204,
                     @task.Rewrite.T207,
                     @task.Rewrite.T210,
                     @task.Rewrite.T301,
                     @task.Rewrite.T303
