        derives_from [
                     @plan.StoriesAndModels.O2,
                     @plan.StoriesAndModels.V2,
                     @plan.StoriesAndModels.C2
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.StoriesAndModels.O2]
        description
            Deliverable: complete service fixtures, resource seeds, and exact dependency-ordered
            recipes.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/testing/fixture/** and co-located tests.
            Evidence: fixture closure, recipe identity, seed, and lease receipts; evidence/T507.md.
            1. Validate fixture service closure and duplicate providers before construction.
            2. Materialize exact providers before consumers and retain production actor leases.
            3. Test repeated recipe identity, transitive refs, seeds, shared actors, and reversed
            cleanup.
            Prerequisites: P1 App/Implementation closure, P2 admission/lease/snapshot owners, and P3
            canonical seed identity/store. T506 supplies the closed Story types.
            Shared-write boundary: T507 owns fixture/recipe modules; T508 consumes their production
            inputs.
        acceptance
            Missing requirements, duplicate providers, foreign/mismatched refs, and dependency
            cycles reject
            before actor creation or external work.
            Providers construct once per Runtime before consumers; exact recipe identity and leases
            persist
            through use; Story leases release in reverse dependency order.
            Seeds neither satisfy services nor bypass production kernels; app-owned actors remain
            Runtime-owned.
            Run fixture/recipe tests and focused type checks; expected: all closure and cleanup
            cases pass.

    T508
        title        Production Story execution and cleanup
        status       draft
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [
                     @T507,
                     @task.Rewrite.T201,
                     @task.Rewrite.T202,
                     @task.Rewrite.T203,
                     @task.Rewrite.T204,
                     @task.Rewrite.T205,
                     @task.Rewrite.T206,
                     @task.Rewrite.T207,
                     @task.Rewrite.T208,
                     @task.Rewrite.T209,
                     @task.Rewrite.T210,
                     @task.Rewrite.T313,
                     @task.Rewrite.T415,
                     @T519,
                     @T521
                     ]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.StoriesAndModels.O3,
                     @plan.StoriesAndModels.V3,
                     @plan.StoriesAndModels.D1,
                     @plan.StoriesAndModels.C1,
                     @plan.StoriesAndModels.Q1,
                     @plan.StoriesAndModels.Q3,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.V2,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.O2,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.V2,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.V4
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.StoriesAndModels.O3]
        description
            Deliverable: one Story.run executor uses production Runtime, deterministic TestClock,
            and
            ordered cleanup for App and machine Stories.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/testing/execution/** and co-located
            tests.
            Evidence: mailbox/time/exit/cleanup proofs; evidence/T508.md.
            1. Construct one fresh production Runtime and isolated in-memory persistence per App
            run.
            2. Process acknowledged commands and ready production work without implicit time
            movement.
            3. Exercise cancellation, maxTurns, pending external work, and each cleanup failure
            lane.
            Prerequisites: P2 runtime owners, P3 integrated actor/store publication, and P4 settled
            Stage 4
            gate T415. T205/T206 remain explicit context-wave decision blockers.
            Local questions: Stories Q1 and Q3 leave the public error members and duration input
            open.
            Keep this Task draft until both owner decisions land; do not invent constructor or
            duration forms.
            Shared-write boundary: T508 owns the executor and clock integration, not evidence
            schema or CLI.
        acceptance
            One executor runs through production bootstrap, admission, mailbox, timers, operations,
            and cleanup.
            Clock movement alone drains no work; process drains only ready work within maxTurns.
            Cancellation closes admission, stops later commands, preserves partial evidence, and
            waits for
            finalizers. Every finalizer runs once in deterministic order; failure truth remains
            primary.
            No successful result follows cleanup failure; all owned Cause and cleanup diagnostics
            remain.
            Run focused production Story/TestClock tests; expected: every Plan V3 lane passes.

    T509
        title        Atomic Story checkpoints and end evidence
        status       draft
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [
                     @T508,
                     @task.Rewrite.T210,
                     @task.Rewrite.T313,
                     @task.Rewrite.T403,
                     @task.Rewrite.T408
                     ]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.StoriesAndModels.O4,
                     @plan.StoriesAndModels.V4,
                     @plan.StoriesAndModels.D3,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O3,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.V3,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O3,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V3,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.O2,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.V2
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.StoriesAndModels.O4]
        description
            Deliverable: checkpoints and run.end capture the exact Story closure at one committed
            cut.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/testing/evidence/** and co-located
            tests.
            Evidence: membership, race, failure-truth, and immutable-read proofs; evidence/T509.md.
            1. Capture the focused machine or exact App recipe/ref closure and required published
            facts.
            2. Reuse Runtime publication and persistence capture laws without using durability
            membership.
            3. Race actor/store/context publication and test prior checkpoints after later failures.
            Prerequisites: P2 actor snapshots, P3 actor/store publication, P4 context-closed
            capture, and
            bounded evidence sinks. Story membership stays Story-owned.
            Shared-write boundary: T509 owns Story evidence selection; T408 owns accepted evidence
            ordering.
        acceptance
            Capture includes exactly the target closure, one StoreState revision, committed actor
            snapshots,
            pending work, TestClock time, issues, and accepted evidence prefix.
            Concurrent cuts or suspended context debt fail retryably; no partial or fabricated end
            appears.
            Lookup uses copied evidence only, performs no live work, and retains no resume
            authority.
            Earlier checkpoints remain immutable after later failure; cleanup failure cannot return
            success.
            Run capture race and failure tests; expected: exact membership and truthful failure
            pass.

    T510
        title       Pure Story model traversal
        status      draft
        priority    medium
        blocked_by  [@T506, @task.Rewrite.T102, @task.Rewrite.T106, @T520]
        description
            Deliverable: pure candidate-order BFS/DFS traversal over a fresh command-empty machine
            Story.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/testing/model/traversal/** and
            independent oracle tests.
            Evidence: oracle, bound, purity, key-defect, and type receipts; evidence/T510.md.
            1. Implement only the accepted shortest/simple path rules and call-local candidate
            events.
            2. Compare results with an independent small-graph oracle across cycles, keys, and
            bounds.
            3. Prove invalid keys throw synchronously without partial results or acquired authority.
            Prerequisites: T506 defines the base Story; P1 owns machine transitions and canonical
            keys.
            This pure slice deliberately has no P2-P4 blocker.
            Shared-write boundary: T510 owns pure traversal and oracle tests; T511 owns live parity
            checks only.
            Local questions: Stories Q2 and Q4 leave explored counting and the predicted state
            member open.
            Keep the Task draft and do not infer either public shape.
        acceptance
            Zero-step path and candidate order match the independent oracle for BFS and DFS.
            Depth/limit bounds and truncated/explored outputs follow the settled questions once
            resolved.
            Noncanonical or defective keys throw synchronously with no partial paths.
            Traversal performs no Effect, provider construction, Runtime/actor work, mutation, time
            movement,
            or hidden candidate retention.
            Run pure model oracle/property cases and type checks; expected: exact parity and no
            side effects.

    T511
