                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.CommandLineV2.O1]
        description
            Deliverable: exactly ten CLI leaves parse and gateway-loading leaves use the branded
            value.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/cli/grammar/**, gateway-loader/**, and
            tests.
            Evidence: parser matrix, path/identity failures, and inert discovery tests;
            evidence/T513.md.
            1. Implement the exact grammar, defaults, repeated-option rejection, and selector
            parsing.
            2. Resolve project root and gateway under the specified trusted local-code boundary.
            3. Test artifact-only commands with a gateway that fails if imported.
            Prerequisites: P1 initial CLI/package route and T512 gateway. Artifact semantics remain
            owned
            by InspectionAndArtifacts; command grammar remains CLI-owned.
            Shared-write boundary: T513 owns grammar and trusted loader files; artifact and process
            behavior stay with T514/T515.
        acceptance
            Only the ten accepted leaves/options parse; unknown, repeated, conflicting, and deleted
            forms
            fail as usage errors.
            Gateway path escape and package identity mismatch reject before registry access;
            temporary
            bundles are removed on success, failure, and interruption.
            Artifact-only commands never load gateway code; list/describe/build/check do not
            construct
            Runtime, Fixture, actor, sink, or executor.
            Run focused parser/loader tests; expected: exact grammar and inert discovery pass.

    T514
        title        CLI artifact commands and atomic publication
        status       draft
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [
                     @T513,
                     @task.Rewrite.T107,
                     @task.Rewrite.T407,
                     @task.Rewrite.T409,
                     @task.Rewrite.T410,
                     @task.Rewrite.T412
                     ]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.CommandLineV2.O2,
                     @plan.CommandLineV2.V2,
                     @plan.CommandLineV2.D1,
                     @plan.CommandLineV2.D2,
                     @plan.CommandLineV2.C1,
                     @plan.CommandLineV2.C2,
                     @plan.CommandLineV2.C3,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O2,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O4,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O6,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V2,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V4,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V6,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.Q2
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.CommandLineV2.O2]
        description
            Deliverable: behavior and trace artifact-only commands use canonical bounded schemas and
            atomic destination publication.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/cli/artifacts/** and co-located tests.
            Evidence: bounds, schema, preflight, comparison, and atomic-write receipts;
            evidence/T514.md.
            1. Implement build/render/diff/check and summarize/proof/diff over owner projections.
            2. Preflight destinations before Runtime acquisition and use the shared codec for all
            input.
            3. Gate commits so pre-commit failures preserve old or absent output.
            Prerequisites: P1 T107 shared codec, P4 bounded envelopes/schemas/comparison, and T407
            final
            call forms. No CLI-owned schema or comparison semantics are added.
            Local question: InspectionAndArtifacts Q2 leaves final call forms open. Keep this Task
            draft.
            Shared-write boundary: T514 owns artifact command files; T513 owns grammar/loader and
            T515 owns Story process behavior.
        acceptance
            Only the shared structural codec decides bounds, malformed input, and canonical bytes.
            Artifact-only commands execute no gateway or application code.
            Destination preflight precedes any Runtime acquisition; failed pre-commit writes
            preserve prior
            bytes or absence. Comparison keeps completeness, ordering, and equality semantics from
            P4.
            Run CLI artifact tests for malformed/oversized/gzip input, symlinks, races,
            flush/close, and
            pre/post-commit failures; expected: atomicity and canonical diagnostics pass.

