            trace,
            signals, and exit status.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/cli/story-run/** and co-located tests.
            Evidence: result projection, interruption, signal, sink, and exit receipts;
            evidence/T515.md.
            1. Invoke the package-private Story executor without creating a CLI execution model.
            2. Project complete/partial failure, cleanup, and accepted/drained prefixes from its
            result.
            3. Test SIGINT/SIGTERM before and after trace commit and preserve ordered secondary
            failures.
            Prerequisites: T508/T509 production execution/evidence, T512 gateway, T514 artifacts,
            and P1
            diagnostic ownership. The CLI owns only final process projection.
            Local question: Stories Q1 leaves FlowStoryExecutionError readonly members and types
            open.
            Keep this Task draft; do not invent the public error envelope.
            Shared-write boundary: T515 owns Story-result process output/signals/exits; T514 owns
            artifact operations and T516 owns installed-binary proof.
        acceptance
            Story CLI and StoryPlan use one executor, checkpoints, run.end, failure, diagnostics,
            cleanup,
            and private evidence model.
            A first signal closes admission, awaits finalization, publishes truthful partial bytes
            only when
            commit succeeds, and exits 130/143. Pre-commit failure preserves old or absent output.
            The result controls text/JSON, sink diagnostics, and exit; complete traces alone
            satisfy proof.
            Run source CLI integration tests with success, runtime failure, cleanup failure, and
            signals;
            expected: exact result and commit/exit truth in each lane.

    T516
        title       Fresh installed CLI binary and packed parity
        status      draft
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T513, @T514, @T515, @T522, @task.Rewrite.T601]
        satisfies   [@plan.CommandLineV2.O4]
        description
            Deliverable: a fresh installed package binary matches source and packed consumer
            behavior.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/test/packed/cli/** and gate scripts owned
            there.
            Evidence: package revision, install receipt, command outputs, exits, and signal results;
            evidence/T516.md.
            1. Build with the pinned package command and install that fresh output into an isolated
            consumer.
            2. Run behavior, Story, and trace commands against source and installed binary fixtures.
            3. Compare text/JSON, bytes, diagnostics, signals, and exits under the same inputs.
            Prerequisites: CLI leaf implementations and T601 package binary/route configuration. No
            stale
            dist or previously installed package counts as evidence.
            Shared-write boundary: T516 owns isolated installed-binary consumer tests only; CLI
            defects return to T513/T514/T515.
        acceptance
            Build and install a fresh package revision into an isolated consumer; stale dist or a 
            previously installed package is not evidence. Compare source and installed results 
            across the full CommandLine V4 matrix: every supported leaf and 
            malformed/unknown/duplicate-flag grammar lane; trusted loader containment, exact 
            package identity, and gateway failure; text/JSON bytes, stdout/stderr routing, and each 
            specified exit; stdin rules and size bounds; atomic artifact publication on success and 
            failure; Story evidence/checkpoints and trace output; cleanup failure and 
            SIGINT/SIGTERM. For each positive lane assert matching result bytes and exit; for each 
            rejection/failure lane assert the same diagnostic and exit, no partial artifact 
            replacement, and no domain work where the Plan requires inert rejection. Run the pinned 
            package build, packed-consumer checks, and isolated fresh-binary vectors; expected: 
            every source/installed lane matches.

