            descriptors,
            machines, modules, Apps, fixtures, Stories, and models.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/test/requirements-carriers/** only.
            Evidence: positive/negative declarations, inferred unions, and compiler results;
            evidence/T518.md.
            1. Extend the P1 static carrier matrix through complete fixtures, inferred Stories, and
            model
            values; preserve the exact consumer requirement union.
            2. Assert covariance and removal of only Flow-owned Scope; providers never erase the
            carrier.
            3. Reject missing/remaining requirements, duplicate identities, and excessive recursive
            expansion.
            Prerequisites: T104 establishes static carriers; T506/T507/T510 provide the public
            Story,
            fixture, and model values used by consumers.
            Local question: Q4 leaves one predicted snapshot member open. Tests must not read that
            member;
            the Questions do not alter RequirementsOf, but the model declaration stays draft until
            settled.
            Shared-write boundary: this Task adds consumer fixtures only; API carriers stay with
            owner Tasks.
        acceptance
            RequirementsOf preserves the exact union and covariance across all seven carrier levels.
            Complete fixture providers do not replace inferred requirements with never or provider
            branding.
            Only Flow-owned Scope is removed; accepted strict isolated declarations compile without
            any,
            assertion erasure, or excessive instantiation.
            Missing and remaining requirements fail where expected; duplicate providers reject.
            Run the isolated requirements-carrier type suite; expected: all positive and negative
            cases pass.

