    T522
        title        Dispatch CLI commands through one private result
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T512, @T513, @T514, @T515]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.CommandLineV2.O1,
                     @plan.CommandLineV2.O3,
                     @plan.CommandLineV2.V1,
                     @plan.CommandLineV2.V3
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.CommandLineV2.O1, @plan.CommandLineV2.O3]
        description
            Deliverable: one top-level dispatcher owns accepted CLI invocation, help/version, story
            list/describe, and one private result that controls text/JSON, stdout/stderr, and exit.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/cli/dispatch/** and co-located tests.
            Evidence: exact leaf dispatch, result parity, stream routing, and exit tests; 
            evidence/T522.md.
            1. Dispatch only the closed ten-leaf grammar to the gateway or owner command modules.
            2. Keep artifact leaves in T514 and Story run in T515; no parallel CLI execution model.
            3. Prove story list/describe, help/version, result formatting, and process output.
            Prerequisites: T512 gateway, T513 parser/loading, T514 artifact leaves, and T515 Story
            result projection. T601 consumes this settled bin/dispatcher route.
        acceptance
            Each accepted leaf dispatches exactly once through its named owner and one private 
            result
            determines text/JSON and stdout/stderr. Story list/describe use the trusted gateway;
            help/version remain conventional unversioned text.
            Unknown flags, duplicate stdin operands, malformed commands, and gateway load failures
            produce their specified result/exit without domain work. Run dispatcher unit and process
            tests; expected: exact leaf/result parity and no alternate history or execution model.
